WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.240
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:23.240
to air in 2022. Speaking to Deadline after
the Emmy ceremony, HBO president Casey Bloys

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:28.510
also confirmed that work on the show continues
with casting roles currently undergoing.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:33.250
House of the Dragon will begin filming at
the beginning of 2021 and will air sometime

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.550
in 2022.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.200
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.350
It is the main reason Martin did not yet finish
the Winds of Winter book as he postponed writing

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.690
Winds of Winter to write Fire And Blood because
they knew this would be a material for a Game

00:00:50.690 --> 00:01:51.500
of Thrones 
successor show.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.810
House of the Dragon will start with a build-up
towards the Dance of the Dragons and early

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:00.160
seasons will cover the Dance itself. Later
seasons, however, will be based on George

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:05.120
RR Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And Blood
volume 2 book that will continue with Queen

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.940
Rhaenyra's son King Aegon lll reign and will
include Blackfyre rebellion and go all the

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:14.800
way to the end of the Targaryen dynasty, to
Robert’s Rebellion, including the rebellion

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.080
itself.
“If you’d like to know a bit more of what

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.280
the show will be about… well, I can’t
actually spill those beans,” Martin teased

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.040
in his blog, “but you might want to pick
up a copy of two anthologies I did with Gardner

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:31.120
Dozois, Dangerous Women, and Rogues and then
move on to Archmaester Gyldayn’s history,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.080
Fire &amp; Blood.”
Dangerous Women includes what press materials

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.340
describe as a “35,000-word novella” by
Martin called “The Princess and the Queen,

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.530
or, the Blacks and the Greens,” which is
“about the Dance of the Dragons, the vast

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.870
civil war that tore Westeros apart nearly
two centuries before the events of A Game

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.660
of Thrones.”
The Greens were the faction during the Dance

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:55.959
of the Dragons that supported the claim of
Aegon ll Targaryen, their rivals being the

00:02:55.959 --> 00:03:00.580
Blacks, who supported the claim of Rhaenyra
Targaryen. Both were named for the color of

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:05.190
their clothes worn during one tourney.
Rogues, meanwhile, includes Martin’s story

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:10.090
“The Rogue Prince, or, a King’s Brother,”
which chronicles “the early life, adventures,

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:15.140
misdeeds, and marriages of Prince Daemon Targaryen,”
considered “one of the biggest rogues in

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.520
the entire history of Ice and Fire.”
Finally, the novel Fire &amp; Blood, released

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:24.980
in November 2018, is the first novel of a
two-part history of the Targaryens in Westeros.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:29.540
“Centuries before the events of A Game of
Thrones, House Targaryen — the only family

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:34.660
of dragonlords to survive the Doom of Valyria
— took up residence on Dragonstone,” according

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:39.020
to the book’s description on the author’s
site. “Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:43.890
the legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator
of the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:48.349
the generations of Targaryens who fought to
hold that iconic seat, all the way up to the

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:53.610
civil war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
In addition to this, few casting calls have

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:58.340
been known, I’m speaking of that of Daemon
Targaryen, the Rogue Prince, further confirming

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:02.470
that the House of the Dragon will be about
Dance of the Dragons, the Targaryen civil

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.690
war.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:10.950
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.050
producer.
I get many questions from fans asking if they

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:18.269
need to even watch the show when they just
finished Fire And Blood book.

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:21.810
The answer is a huge yes.
Not only will there be differences between

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:26.210
the books and the show like it was with Game
of Thrones, but after reading Fire And Blood

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.770
book, you still don't know how most of the
events really played out.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.210
Some would think that you could just read
the book Fire &amp; Blood to know what will happen

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:38.430
in the show based on that very same book but
that's far from truth. Why?

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:43.520
Because Fire And Blood is not a non-conventional
novel, it is imaginary history book, and according

00:04:43.520 --> 00:05:01.370
to George RR Martin himself, not very accurate

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:25.250
at that.
Because while Fire And blood book was written

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:30.720
by George RR Martin, it wasn't written from
him as facts, but rather through the perspective

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:35.990
of the Citadel's Archmaester Gyldayn who gathered
all the info and as many different sources

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:41.300
as he could and used it to write a book about
the Targaryen history. Some info is fake,

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:45.889
some info is true, some info is semi-true.
No one will know for a fact what was happening

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:50.120
in the real history until the House of the
Dragon airs in 2022.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:57.830
The show unlike the book will contain truth,
it will depict what actually happened, not

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.440
the changed history, fake or semi-true, not
what might or might not have happened.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:04.090
Fire &amp; Blood is a complete history of House
Targaryen written by George R. R. Martin from

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:09.449
a perspective of Archmaester Gyldayn who wrote
it many decades after the events took place.

00:06:09.449 --> 00:06:17.090
Sure, most of the main events such as battles
and deaths probably did happen, but as Gyldayn

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:25.370
says it in the books, the full truth about
what happened behind close doors, in the privacy

00:06:25.370 --> 00:08:31.789
of stairwells, council rooms, and 

00:08:31.789 --> 00:08:36.830
bedchambers he does not fully know and he
turns to many different sources which usually

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:41.050
differ from one another.
He looks into the course of chronicles laid

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:46.990
down by Grand Maester Runciter and his successors
and many court documents as well.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:50.880
Gyldayn looks into accounts written decades
later by the children and grandchildren of

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.680
those caught up in the events of these times.
Whilst there are undoubtedly of use, so much

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:00.459
time has passed between the event and the
recording that many confusions and contradictions

00:09:00.459 --> 00:09:04.490
have inevitably crept in.
Unfortunately, this is also true for Gyldayn's

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:08.910
two accounts by firsthand observers that have
come down to him.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:12.690
Septon Eustace who served in the royal sept
in the Red Keep during much of this time and

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:17.660
spent much time as a confidant and confessor
to King Viserys and his queens. His account

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:23.620
is biased, favoring Aegon II over Rhaenyra.
Second account is based upon the verbal account

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:28.870
of the court fool Mushroom who was present
at court for all of them; for King Viserys,

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:33.970
Princess and Queen Rhaenyra and both King
Aegons, the Second and the Third.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:38.610
During his reign, King Baelor I Targaryen
had Mushroom's book burned on account of its

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:42.190
scandalous content.
There are several main sources for historical

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:47.140
information on the Dance of the Dragons, which
are frequently at odds with each other.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:51.779
Gyldayn also uses source written by Grand
Maester Orwyle, who had served King Aegon

00:09:51.779 --> 00:09:56.520
II Targaryenon his council and was arrested
by the forces of Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen

00:09:56.520 --> 00:10:02.270
when she took the city. Orwyle wrote his account
while locked away in the black cells. Uncertain

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:06.010
about whether or not he would survive the
war, he attempted to paint himself in the

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:09.690
best light possible.
Grand Maester Munkun's The Dance of the Dragons,

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:14.580
A True Telling was based on Orwyle's account.
Using all these sources which often differ

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:19.410
from each other, archmaester Gyldayn wrote
his work, Fire And Blood, his work about the

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:23.730
history of House Targaryen.
This format brings up Martin's major thematic

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:28.820
point about the uncertainty of memory, and
history being written by the winners. Neither

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:33.620
side truly won the war, and the decades after
the war, both sides wrote their own biased

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:38.690
history books trying to put their actions
in a better light. Histories written by the

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:42.580
Greens depict Aegon II in good light and Rhaenyra
in bad.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:45.580
On the other hand, histories written by the
Blacks do otherwise.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:50.020
We will know exactly what happened in this
time period when the show comes out, and that's

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:53.990
why you cannot just read Fire And Blood book
and think you would know what actually happen

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:58.370
or what will happen on the show. Books are
written by Archmaester decades and decades

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:02.950
after the events happened, using many sources
that in most cases are very different from

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:05.990
each other and most of them are biased as
well.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:09.970
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:15.450
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:18.519
I's throne.
Both of them thought they belonged on the

00:11:18.519 --> 00:11:22.900
Iron Throne. When people started declaring
for one of them or the other, their fight

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:28.800
divided the kingdoms in two. Targaryens fought
Targaryens, bothers fought brothers, dragons

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:33.520
fought dragons. By the time it was over, thousands
were dead. The conflict would prove to be

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.120
incredibly destructive for not only House
Targaryen, but large parts of Westeros as

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:43.550
well. In addition, it devastated the Targaryen's
dragon population, ultimately leading to their

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:47.540
extinction within a few decades.
They never truly recovered.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:52.010
By the end of the reign of King Viserys I
Targaryen, twenty dragons were alive. The

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:56.890
majority of these died during the civil war
called the Dance of the Dragons, which began

00:11:56.890 --> 00:12:04.210
in 129 AC and lasted until mid 131 AC.
The show won't jump straight into the fighting,

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:09.170
it will start with a few episodes of the prelude
to the Targaryen civil war, with King Viserys

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:14.010
l likely dying after a few episodes, which
is just enough to introduce us with all the

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:19.089
characters and which side they support as
the future heir, as well as to set up all

00:12:19.089 --> 00:12:23.310
the animosity at the court.
King Viserys I Targaryen had three children

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:29.480
by his first queen, Aemma Arryn, but only
one, Princess Rhaenyra, survived to adulthood.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:34.460
Lacking a son to succeed him, Viserys began
to train Rhaenyra to be his heir, named her

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:39.490
his heir and Rhaenyra soon acquired a support
of hundreds of lords and landed knights.

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:45.339
The king remarried in 106 AC, this time to
Alicent Hightower, and had four more children:

00:12:45.339 --> 00:12:50.950
Aegon, Helaena, Aemond, and Daeron.
In 111 AC, a great tourney was held at King's

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:56.280
Landing on the fifth anniversary of Viserys's
marriage to Alicent. During the opening feast,

00:12:56.280 --> 00:13:00.959
Queen Alicent wore a green gown, while Princess
Rhaenyra dressed in the red and black of House

00:13:00.959 --> 00:13:06.470
Targaryen. The note was taken, and soon all
of Rhaenyra's supporters started wearing black

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:11.360
clothing, while all of Alicent's followers
started wearing green. Over the years, the

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:16.660
popular names applied to both factions were
inspired by the colors they wore: Rhaenyra's

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:21.100
supporters were called "the Blacks", and Aegon
II's supporters were called "the Greens".

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:26.899
Viserys I strengthened Rhaenyra's place in
the succession by marrying her in 114 AC to

00:13:26.899 --> 00:13:32.620
Ser Laenor Velaryon - who himself had Targaryen
blood through his mother, Princess Rhaenys.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:38.120
Rhaenyra gave birth to three sons—Jacaerys,
Lucerys, and Joffrey Velaryon—during her

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:42.329
marriage, although there were rumors that
the father of these princes was not Laenor,

00:13:42.329 --> 00:13:48.090
but Ser Harwin Strong. After Laenor was murdered
in Spicetown in 120 AC, Rhaenyra married her

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:54.810
uncle, infamous Rogue Prince, Prince Daemon
Targaryen, younger brother to Viserys I. Her

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:59.769
sons by him were Aegon the Younger—called
so to distinguish him from his uncle, Alicent's

00:13:59.769 --> 00:14:03.720
Aegon, who on occasion was called Aegon the
Elder—and Viserys.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:08.630
The relationship between Rhaenyra and Alicent
declined early in Alicent's marriage to Viserys,

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:13.880
since both ladies had been trying to be the
realm's first lady, and there could only be

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:19.360
one. Alicent's father, Ser Otto Hightower,
had also disliked Rhaenyra's second husband,

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:22.740
Prince Daemon, since the beginning of Viserys's
reign.

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:28.200
The war began when King Viserys I died. His
designated heir for many years had been his

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:34.960
only surviving child by his first wife, his
daughter Rhaenyra. Since Viserys I later remarried,

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:39.510
however, and had several younger children
by his second wife, Alicent Hightower, the

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:44.089
eldest of which was Rhaenyra's half-brother
Aegon II. The Seven Kingdoms had never had

00:14:44.089 --> 00:14:48.959
a Ruling Queen before, and many were troubled
by the thought of Rhaenyra succeeding to the

00:14:48.959 --> 00:14:54.390
throne. By the inheritance laws of the Andals,
a younger brother succeeds ahead of an elder

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:59.740
daughter, but the Targaryens had never formalized
royal inheritance laws for their new realm

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:05.300
after the War of Conquest 130 years before.
Viserys I, however, had extracted oaths of

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:09.310
fealty from the major lords of the realm that
Rhaenyra would succeed him.

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:15.459
The same day that Viserys I died, Aegon II's
followers, the Greens, staged a coup, and

00:15:15.459 --> 00:15:21.139
he was soon crowned in King's Landing. Rhaenyra,
as the Princess of Dragonstone, had her powerbase

00:15:21.139 --> 00:15:27.370
on Dragonstone island, where she responded
by being crowned queen and declaring Aegon

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:29.910
a traitor.
Aegon II's main supporters were his mother

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:36.110
Alicent's family, the powerful House Hightower
that rules Oldtown as well as the Lannisters.

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:41.100
Rhaenyra's main supporters were her first
husband's family, House Velaryon, as well

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:46.191
as her mother's family, House Arryn and her
uncle and future husband, the most dangerous

00:15:46.191 --> 00:15:51.460
man in the Seven Kingdoms and the most experienced
commander, Daemon Targaryen.

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:55.620
The Blacks were mostly in the northeastern
half of Westeros, while the Greens were mostly

00:15:55.620 --> 00:16:00.610
in the southwestern half. Dorne was not yet
part of the realm and remained neutral during

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:05.380
the war. The Blacks included the Arryns, the
Starks, and the Tullys (along with most if

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:10.980
not all of the Riverlords, even the Freys).
The Starks felt bound by honor to remain true

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:16.810
to the fealty oaths they had made to Rhaenyra
when her father was still alive. Major Greens

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:22.650
included the Hightowers and Lannisters. Rhaenyra
had thought the Baratheons would support her,

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:28.010
but in what she saw as a major betrayal they
sided with Aegon II. The Greens faced their

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:32.470
own betrayal, however: they had assumed that
all of the Reach would side with the Greens,

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:37.639
but instead the northern half of the Reach
sided with the Blacks. Even some of the Hightowers'

00:16:37.639 --> 00:16:42.589
own direct vassals in the south sided with
the Blacks. The Tyrells remained officially

00:16:42.589 --> 00:16:46.470
neutral throughout the war.
The Greens had thought that the Greyjoys would

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:51.210
join them - not realizing that the great wealth
they controlled ironically made them a more

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:56.430
enticing target. Seeing little profit in sailing
all the way to the eastern side of Westeros

00:16:56.430 --> 00:17:02.100
to raid the modest lands of the Vale or Dragonstone,
the Greyjoys nominally sided with the Blacks

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:06.480
in order to raid the Lannister-Hightower lands
along the eastern coast.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:10.569
Despite the Greens controlling the wealthier
lands of Westeros, the Blacks had the advantage

00:17:10.569 --> 00:17:16.139
of control of the seas. The Greens only had
the Redwyne Fleet to rely on for naval power,

00:17:16.139 --> 00:17:20.799
while - through House Velaryon - Rhaenyra's
forces controlled most of the Royal Fleet.

00:17:20.799 --> 00:17:24.509
After the Greyjoys sided with the Blacks,
however, the Iron Fleet tied up the Redwynes

00:17:24.509 --> 00:17:29.491
in their raids on the west coast, giving the
Blacks free run of the eastern coast. The

00:17:29.491 --> 00:17:34.399
Greens attempted to counter this by allying
with the Kingdom of the Three Daughters (an

00:17:34.399 --> 00:17:38.919
alliance of Lys, Myr, and Tyrosh), whose fleet
assaulted Rhaenyra's fleets in the massive

00:17:38.919 --> 00:17:44.139
Battle of the Gullet. A third of the Velaryon
fleet was lost, but two-thirds of the Three

00:17:44.139 --> 00:17:49.460
Daughters fleet was destroyed, and the survivors
withdrew from the rest of the war. Overall,

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:54.200
this meant that despite the Greens' numerical
superiority, they had to slowly struggle to

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:58.899
march their armies over land to attack the
Blacks, instead of being able to quickly move

00:17:58.899 --> 00:18:03.059
their larger armies by sea.
After Rhaenyra was crowned Queen by Daemon

00:18:03.059 --> 00:18:08.070
at Dragonstone and declared her half brother
traitor, King Aegon II declared Rhaenyra and

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:13.749
Daemon traitors as well. After being persuaded
by his mother, Alicent and sister, Helaena,

00:18:13.749 --> 00:18:19.590
Aegon dispatched Grand Maester Orwyle to Dragonstone
with a retinue under a peace banner, offering

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:24.769
Rhaenyra generous terms, but was refused.
Rhaenyra's sons departed on their dragons

00:18:24.769 --> 00:18:30.519
to seek allies and make pacts on her mother's
behalf. Her eldest son, Jacaerys went visiting

00:18:30.519 --> 00:18:35.619
the Arryns of the Eyrie, the Manderlys of
White Harbor, and the Starks of Winterfell.

00:18:35.619 --> 00:18:40.200
Rhaenyra's second son, Lucerys, traveled to
Baratheons at Storm's End.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:44.600
Prince Daemon led the blacks' attack on Harrenhal,
which was conquered without bloodshed-The

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:51.350
castellan, Ser Simon Strong, yielded when
he saw Daemon's dragon Caraxes. This conquest

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:56.289
led to victories of the blacks at the Burning
Mill and Stone Hedge and allowed the river

00:18:56.289 --> 00:19:01.039
lords to gather at Harrenhal.
In the meantime, Jacaerys gained Lady Arryn

00:19:01.039 --> 00:19:06.989
and the Lords Manderly, Borrell and Sunderland,
and Cregan Starkto Rhaenyra's cause, with

00:19:06.989 --> 00:19:10.350
Lord Stark allying through the Pact of Ice
and Fire.

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:15.139
Lucerys flew to Storm's End, arriving before
a gathering storm. He found Prince Aemond

00:19:15.139 --> 00:19:20.480
and his dragon Vhagar already present. Aemond
tried to get Lucerys into a fight, insulting

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:26.130
him, calling him a Strong bastard, but Lucerys,
who sworn to his mother not to fight, refused

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:32.279
him. He delivered his message to Lord Borros
Baratheon, but was refused and told to leave.

00:19:32.279 --> 00:19:36.679
Borros prevented Aemond from attacking his
cousin in the castle, but did allow for the

00:19:36.679 --> 00:19:41.730
prince to follow him. Mounted on his dragon,
Aemond caught up with Lucerys during a raging

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:47.119
storm. The fight between the two dragons did
not last long. Vhagar, being five times bigger,

00:19:47.119 --> 00:19:52.720
had the advantage, and Arrax fell broken.
His head and neck washed ashore three days

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:58.220
later, along with the corpse of Lucerys.
Rhaenyra collapsed when learning of Lucerys's

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:02.779
death. Prince Daemon, at Harrenhal, sent a
raven to his wife, promising that her son's

00:20:02.779 --> 00:20:06.669
death would be avenged.
Using one of his friends from King's Landing,

00:20:06.669 --> 00:20:11.760
Daemon enlisted the help of a former serjeant
in the City Watch, known now only as Blood,

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:16.659
and a rat-catcher from the Red Keep, known
now only as Cheese. The two sneaked into the

00:20:16.659 --> 00:20:21.309
Red Keep, using secret tunnels and hidden
doors, which brought them into the Tower of

00:20:21.309 --> 00:20:27.270
the Hand. There, Queen Alicent was bound and
gagged, and her bed maid strangled. When Queen

00:20:27.270 --> 00:20:32.440
Helaena and her three children appeared, Blood
and Cheese barred the doors and told Helaena

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:37.820
to choose which of her sons would die. Helaena
reluctantly chose Maelor, but Blood did the

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:42.960
opposite and killed Prince Jaehaerys instead.
The two fled with the prince's head.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:48.029
The war was a stalemate, with many unexpected
victories as well as unexpected losses for

00:20:48.029 --> 00:20:54.071
both sides, with no clear victor emerging.
Even King's Landing itself was attacked, though

00:20:54.071 --> 00:20:59.009
there was no siege - Rhaenyra's new husband
Daemon (her own uncle) had reorganized and

00:20:59.009 --> 00:21:03.919
essentially created the City Watch as it would
later be known, and they remained loyal to

00:21:03.919 --> 00:21:09.359
him. After the Greens foolishly left the capital
city lightly defended to attack Rhaenyra's

00:21:09.359 --> 00:21:14.309
armies gathering at Harrenhal, her forces
on Dragonstone moved against King's Landing,

00:21:14.309 --> 00:21:18.019
and the Gold Cloaks threw the gates open at
their arrival.

00:21:18.019 --> 00:21:23.460
The war eventually degenerated into near-anarchy
as a string of betrayals happened in rapid

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:28.259
succession on both sides. Rival kings started
popping up in different parts of the realm

00:21:28.259 --> 00:21:33.559
- ranging from the Greyjoys behaving functionally
independent to Dragonriders deciding that

00:21:33.559 --> 00:21:39.009
they would make better kings than Rhaenyra
or Aegon II, to even petty street thugs carving

00:21:39.009 --> 00:21:44.619
out their own fiefdoms in King's Landing and
declaring themselves "king" of half the city.

00:21:44.619 --> 00:21:47.539
There is many interesting and legendary side
characters as well.

00:21:47.539 --> 00:21:52.710
We have a combination of Varys and Littlefinger
in Larys Strong being the one in the shadows

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:55.779
orchestrating many events and making kings
rise and fall.

00:21:55.779 --> 00:22:02.229
We also have Melisandre is Alys Rivers, Aemond
Targaryen's mistress and perhaps that's even

00:22:02.229 --> 00:22:08.129
Melisandre herself in her younger days. Alys
sees visions in the flames and has some great

00:22:08.129 --> 00:22:11.820
powers.
Racallio Ryndoon, pirate-king, is another

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:16.049
legendary side character in this story. If
even half the stories about him are true,

00:22:16.049 --> 00:22:20.720
he is probably one of the most insane and
most fascinating characters I've ever read.

00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:25.509
It's a Targaryen civil war so of course Targaryens
and their dragons play the main role in the

00:22:25.509 --> 00:22:30.559
series, but the Starks, Lannisters, Arryns,
Tullys and Hightowers are very important as

00:22:30.559 --> 00:22:33.649
well.
One of the most exciting 1 on 1 fights is

00:22:33.649 --> 00:22:39.210
definitely legendary Daemon Targaryen against
Aemond one-eye that happened above the Gods

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:44.549
Eye and resulted with both men and both their
dragons dying, although Daemon did win a fight

00:22:44.549 --> 00:22:49.629
by piercing his Valyrian steel sword through
Aemond's eye socket but seconds later both

00:22:49.629 --> 00:22:55.909
dragons hit a lake at a rapid speed.
Aemond's body was found but Daemon's was not.

00:22:55.909 --> 00:23:00.610
Historians say Daemon died in this fight but
singers sing of his departure from Westeros

00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:04.919
to live his days out in Essos.
I'm not going to talk about every single event,

00:23:04.919 --> 00:23:08.940
but this all of the things I mentioned is
what essentially kick-started this Dance of

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:13.890
the Dragons, referring to Viserys's death,
animosity between the Greens and the Blacks

00:23:13.890 --> 00:23:19.330
and especially the first fight where Rhaenyra
lost her son did it turn into a violent, long,

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:25.179
bloody tale full of revenge, violence, lust,
love and dragon-to-dragon aerial battles.

00:23:25.179 --> 00:23:30.330
The civil war lasted two years and gutted
the Seven Kingdoms, with dragons burning out

00:23:30.330 --> 00:23:36.169
vast swaths of the countryside, and entire
towns reduced to ashes. The devastation was

00:23:36.169 --> 00:23:39.020
so great that it took a full generation to
recover.

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:44.960
At the start of the war, there were 20 living
dragons: 9 older and huge dragons, 8 younger

00:23:44.960 --> 00:23:50.590
dragons still large enough to be ridden to
war, and 3 hatchlings too small to ride. By

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:55.489
the end of the war, all but three had died.
Another dragon was hatched near the end of

00:23:55.489 --> 00:24:00.419
the war, bringing the total number of surviving
dragons to four. None of them would live for

00:24:00.419 --> 00:24:05.219
long, and there were too few dragons left
to maintain a stable breeding population.

00:24:05.219 --> 00:24:11.261
The last dragon, said to be a stunted creature,
died only 33 years after the war ended, later

00:24:11.261 --> 00:24:16.849
in the reign of Rhaenery's son King Aegon
lll for which he became known as "Aegon the

00:24:16.849 --> 00:24:21.100
Dragonbane"
Twenty major battles, even more, smaller battles,

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:26.630
and even more betrayals, turncloaks, and twists.
All of that this Game of Thrones prequel show,

00:24:26.630 --> 00:24:31.039
House of the Dragon, brings in 2022.
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed

00:24:31.039 --> 00:24:35.249
this video and let me know what team you on
in the comment section down below. Team Blacks

00:24:35.249 --> 00:24:35.840
supporting Rhaenyra or team Greens supporting
Aegon?

